--- This module defines status of TEE applications.

--- @kind constants
--- @feature ta-session
fmod APP-STATUS is
  sort AppStatus .

  --- normal: the TA runs.  As in the rules printed in the paper, a rule of a TA (a TA invocation,
  --- an API call, a step of a TEE API function, a shared-memory builtin) fires only in status normal.
  --- outOfMemory: the memory of the TA is exhausted.  Only the memory error rules of the functions
  --- that allocate memory (allocateTransientObject, allocOperation, openPersistentObject,
  --- createPersistent, allocatePersistentObjectEnumerator) fire in this status: the call returns
  --- errorOutOfMemory instead of allocating.  No rule sets the status back to normal, so a TA in
  --- this status stops at its next step that is not such a memory error rule.
  --- panic: the TA has panicked.  A panic rule leaves the call without a return value (it consumes
  --- the reply of the object, or sets api-call to noCall), and no rule of the TA fires in this status
  --- except the ones that answer its client with errorTargetDead.
  op normal : -> AppStatus [ctor] .
  op outOfMemory : -> AppStatus [ctor] .
  op panic : -> AppStatus [ctor] .
endfm

view AppStatus from TRIV to APP-STATUS is
  sort Elt to AppStatus .
endv

--- This module defines a kernel class, modeling the TA kernel.

--- @kind state
--- @feature ta-session
omod TA-KERNEL is
  pr OBJECT-ID .
  pr APP-STATUS .
  pr NAT .
  pr TEE-API-CALL .

  --- The call status (api-call) has the states noCall, init, exec, final and return.
  class TAKernel | status : AppStatus, storage : Oid,
                   os-kernel : Oid, counter : Nat,
                   api-call : CallStatus .
endom

--- This module defines the TA kernel behavior.

--- @kind behavior
--- @feature ta-session
omod TA-KERNEL-BEHAVIOR is
  pr TA-KERNEL .

  var TK : Oid .

--- TrustedApp can be in out-of-memory at any time.

  --- rl [out-of-memory] :
  ---   < TK : TAKernel | status : normal >
  ---   =>
  ---   < TK : TAKernel | status : outOfMemory >
  --- .

endom
